diff --git a/crates/rightkit-http/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-http/CHANGELOG.md
index 7537ef1..0eb2c38 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-http/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-http/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,17 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.3.6 (Unreleased; round-2 gaps, additive, written without a build: not compiled or run)
+
+- **`ClientConfig::on_outcome` and `AttemptOutcome` (rightkit#305 follow-up, CodeRight; also what #658 needs).** An observer that runs after every physical attempt in `Client` and `AsyncClient`, the counterpart of `on_attempt`. `AttemptOutcome { url (redacted), method, attempt, max_attempts, status: Option<u16>, error_class: Option<ErrorClass>, delay: Option<Duration> }`: `status` is set when the attempt got a response, `error_class` when it failed, `delay` is the wait before the next attempt and `None` for the final one. It cannot change the result. An attempt `on_attempt` refused sent nothing and reports no outcome. New field on the non-`#[non_exhaustive]` `ClientConfig` (literals need `..Default::default()`, as for `on_attempt`). Not done: a separate transport-error versus status-error retry budget (`RetryPolicy::transport_backoff`); the observer lets the caller keep its own ladder meanwhile.
+- **`HttpError::request_may_have_been_delivered()` (rightkit#718, GenRight).** `false` only when the error proves nothing was sent: a `Phase::Connect` transport failure or timeout, `InvalidRequest`, `SystemProxyUnsupported`, `AddressDenied`, `HttpsRequired`. `true` for every other kind (later phases, any status, malformed or oversized response, cancellation). It judges one error; a final `InvalidRequest` from the attempt hook refusing a later attempt can follow an earlier attempt that did reach the server (use `on_outcome` for that).
+- **`AddressPolicy::allow_host_of(url)` (rightkit#696, CodeRight).** Pins one host taken from a URL (scheme, userinfo, port, path ignored; IPv6 brackets and trailing dot normalised) and lets it reach any address it resolves to, for a configured LAN, tunnel or self-hosted endpoint. Wraps `allow_if`, so link-local and metadata destinations, `deny_ranges` and `deny_if` still refuse. An unparsable or non-`http(s)` URL changes nothing.
+- **`AddressPolicy::first_party_path_prefix(host, prefix)` (rightkit#744, ScrapeRight).** Limits a host to request paths under a prefix (whole segments; repeat for several prefixes; `/` admits all), checked on the first request and every redirect hop in both clients. A path with a `.`/`..` segment, a backslash, or an encoded `/`, `\` or dot segment is refused (`HttpError::AddressDenied`, nothing sent). It narrows a host and does not admit one.
+- **`format_http_date(SystemTime)` (rightkit#369).** IMF-fixdate (`Sun, 06 Nov 1994 08:49:37 GMT`), the inverse of the `parse_retry_after` date form, for mocks.
+- **`redact_url` and `redact_urls_in_text` are public (rightkit#371, part).** The URL-in-text redaction the crate already applied to its own errors (userinfo, query and fragment removed) is now exported. Redacting OAuth-style `key=value` text outside URLs is not done here.
+- Tests: `tests/outcome_and_scope.rs`, unit tests in `error.rs`, `netpolicy.rs` (`host_pin_and_path_tests`) and `retry.rs`.
+- **Deferred, not implemented:** a TLS-fingerprint / impersonation transport (#744 item 1) and the `fetch`-compatible Tauri bridge for `rightkit-http` (#448 item 3); see the issues.
+- Already present at 0.3.5 and unchanged: `ClientConfig::on_attempt` (#305), `SseDecoder::eager`, `finish`, `has_pending` (#647), `validate_public_https_url` (#374).
+
 ## 0.3.5 (2026-10-17)
 
 - **Public https URL policy (rightkit#374).** `netpolicy::validate_public_https_url(&str) -> Result<(), UrlPolicyError>` (also re-exported from the crate root). It accepts only `https` (any case), no userinfo, a non-empty host that is a public IP literal or a multi-label name, and refuses `localhost`, `*.localhost`, `*.local`, `*.internal`, single-label names, and legacy IPv4 spellings. It reads the string only and does not resolve; the request-time SSRF guard still vets resolved addresses. `UrlPolicyError` is `#[non_exhaustive]`. Tests in `netpolicy::public_url_tests`. Not compiled or run.
